      "notes": "A workload can trust an outside account in a role's trust policy, or share a queue or a secret through its resource policy; this caps both, whatever the policy says. Only sts:AssumeRole: AssumeRoleWithSAML and AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity (IAM Identity Center, GitHub OIDC) carry no organization ID and stay open. AWS services are exempt, so services can still assume their roles. Break-glass is organization principals, so the exemption is moot here.",
      "objective": "trust-perimeter",
      "severity": "Critical",
      "severity_source": "rubric",
      "shared": true,
      "title": "Only organization principals, named trusted accounts or AWS services assume organization roles or reach its SQS queues and Secrets Manager secrets"
